# Self-flashing BIOS updater volume (WIC kickstart).
#
# MBR with a single 60 MiB FAT32 EFI System Partition (--system-id 0xef, the
# type scripts/make-flasher-img.sh's sfdisk wrote; wic would otherwise
# default an MBR vfat partition to 0x6/FAT16) carrying the flasher UKI at
# \EFI\BOOT\BOOTX64.EFI, the removable-media default boot path.
#
# 60 MiB fits the UKI (~40 MiB: Alpine kernel + initramfs + the 8 MiB ROM in
# the overlay) with headroom for kernel growth across Alpine pin bumps.
# Supplying --mkfs-extraopts REPLACES wic's default ("-S 512"), so it is
# restated; "-F 32" forces FAT32, which at 60 MiB with 512-byte clusters
# clears the 65525-cluster FAT32 floor.
#
# Populated from the flasher-staging tree the recipe assembles and passes as
# the default ROOTFS_DIR (WIC_CREATE_EXTRA_ARGS), same mechanism as the rpi5
# image recipes.
#
# Keep the part directive on one line: wic's kickstart parser shlex-splits
# each line and does not join backslash continuations.

bootloader --ptable msdos

part --source rootfs --rootfs-dir=ROOTFS_DIR --fstype=vfat --label NUCFLASH --align 1024 --fixed-size 60M --system-id 0xef --mkfs-extraopts "-S 512 -F 32"
